WEBVTT

00:00.450 --> 00:02.028
- [Instructor] All right,
let's say that we have

00:02.028 --> 00:07.028
the function f of x and it's
equal to two x plus five,

00:07.400 --> 00:10.650
over four minus three x.

00:10.650 --> 00:12.280
And what we wanna do is figure out what

00:12.280 --> 00:14.310
is the inverse of our function.

00:14.310 --> 00:15.459
Pause this video and try to figure

00:15.459 --> 00:17.923
that out before we work on that together.

00:18.760 --> 00:21.220
All right, now let's work on it together.

00:21.220 --> 00:22.612
Just as a reminder of what a function

00:22.612 --> 00:25.260
and an inverse even does,

00:25.260 --> 00:27.159
if this is the domain of a function

00:27.159 --> 00:30.490
and that's the set of all
values that you could input

00:30.490 --> 00:34.370
into the function for x
and get a valid output.

00:34.370 --> 00:35.760
And so let's say you have an x here,

00:35.760 --> 00:37.460
it's a member of the domain.

00:37.460 --> 00:40.700
And if I were to apply the function to it,

00:40.700 --> 00:42.919
or if I were to input
that x into that function.

00:42.919 --> 00:47.420
Then the function is
going to output a value

00:47.420 --> 00:52.420
in the range of the function
and we call that value f of x.

00:52.890 --> 00:56.180
Now an inverse, that goes the other way.

00:56.180 --> 01:00.790
If you were to input the f
of x value into the function

01:00.790 --> 01:03.910
that's going to take us back to x.

01:03.910 --> 01:07.870
So that's exactly what f inverse does.

01:07.870 --> 01:09.800
Now how do we actually
figure out the inverse

01:09.800 --> 01:10.829
of a function especially a function

01:10.829 --> 01:15.410
that's defined with a
rational expression like this.

01:15.410 --> 01:17.750
Well the way that I think about it is,

01:17.750 --> 01:21.440
let's say that y is equal
to our function of x

01:21.440 --> 01:23.537
or y is a function of x so we could say

01:23.537 --> 01:27.550
that y is equal to two x plus five,

01:27.550 --> 01:30.670
over four minus three x.

01:30.670 --> 01:32.263
For our inverse the relationship

01:32.263 --> 01:35.200
between x and y is going to be swapped.

01:35.200 --> 01:37.344
And so in our inverse it's going

01:37.344 --> 01:42.344
to be true that x is going to
be equal to two y plus five,

01:43.680 --> 01:47.060
over four minus three y.

01:47.060 --> 01:49.200
And then to be able to express this

01:49.200 --> 01:51.716
as a function of x, to say
that what is y as a function

01:51.716 --> 01:56.020
of x for our inverse we
now have to solve for y.

01:56.020 --> 01:57.450
So it's just a little bit of algebra here.

01:57.450 --> 01:59.940
So let's see if we can do that.

01:59.940 --> 02:01.123
So the first thing that I would do

02:01.123 --> 02:06.123
is multiply both sides of this
equation by four minus 3 y.

02:07.370 --> 02:09.685
If we do that, on the left
hand side we are going

02:09.685 --> 02:12.870
to get x times each of these terms.

02:12.870 --> 02:16.680
So we're going to get
four x minus three yx

02:17.990 --> 02:19.450
and then that's going to be equal to

02:19.450 --> 02:20.917
on the right hand side,
since we multiplied

02:20.917 --> 02:22.720
by the denominator here we're just going

02:22.720 --> 02:24.050
to be left with the numerator.

02:24.050 --> 02:26.960
It's going to be equal to two y plus five.

02:26.960 --> 02:27.793
And this could be a
little bit intimidating

02:27.793 --> 02:30.710
'cause we're seeing xs and
ys, what are we trying to do,

02:30.710 --> 02:33.920
remember we're trying to solve for y.

02:33.920 --> 02:36.490
So let's gather all
the y terms on one side

02:36.490 --> 02:39.030
and all the non-y terms on the other side.

02:39.030 --> 02:41.910
So let's get rid of this two y here.

02:41.910 --> 02:44.250
Actually, well I could go either way.

02:44.250 --> 02:45.440
Let's get rid of this two y here,

02:45.440 --> 02:49.590
so let's subtract two y from both sides.

02:49.590 --> 02:53.050
And let's get rid of this four
x from the left hand side,

02:53.050 --> 02:57.270
so let's subtract four x from both sides.

02:57.270 --> 02:59.820
And then what're we going to be left with.

02:59.820 --> 03:03.156
On the left hand side
we're left with minus

03:03.156 --> 03:07.600
or negative five, or actually
it would be this way,

03:07.600 --> 03:12.600
it would be negative three yx minus two y.

03:12.630 --> 03:13.538
And you might say hey where is this going,

03:13.538 --> 03:15.490
but I'll show you in a second,

03:15.490 --> 03:17.077
is equal to, those cancel out

03:17.077 --> 03:21.350
and we're gonna have five minus four x.

03:21.350 --> 03:24.290
Now once again we are
trying to solve for y.

03:24.290 --> 03:26.680
So let's factor out a y here,

03:26.680 --> 03:29.670
and then we are going to have y,

03:29.670 --> 03:33.410
times negative three x minus two

03:33.410 --> 03:36.460
is equal to five minus four x.

03:36.460 --> 03:38.560
And now this is the homestretch.

03:38.560 --> 03:40.684
We can just divide both
sides of this equation

03:40.684 --> 03:43.206
by negative three x minus two

03:43.206 --> 03:46.540
and we're going to get y is equal

03:46.540 --> 03:51.540
to five minus four x, over
negative three x minus two.

03:53.200 --> 03:54.606
Now another way that
you could express this

03:54.606 --> 03:55.873
is you could multiply both the numerator

03:55.873 --> 03:57.870
and the denominator by negative one,

03:57.870 --> 03:59.170
that won't change the value.

03:59.170 --> 04:01.170
And then you would get, you would get

04:01.170 --> 04:03.210
in the numerator four x minus five,

04:03.210 --> 04:06.860
and in the denominator you
would get a three x plus two.

04:06.860 --> 04:07.990
So there you have it.

04:07.990 --> 04:10.900
Our f inverse as a function of x,

04:10.900 --> 04:12.750
which we could say is equal to this y

04:12.750 --> 04:15.163
is equal to this right over there.
